 "prompt": "Edit the FIRST image. It is an animator's layout sheet: 8 posing mannequins in a 4x2 grid, the 8 successive drawings of ONE run cycle (reading left to right, top row then bottom row). Paint the character from the SECOND image (his model sheet) over every mannequin, as 8 finished key drawings by the same animator. The second image only shows what he looks like: do not copy its standing figures, its poses or its arrangement; the result holds exactly the 8 figures of the first image, each in its mannequin's pose and place, and nothing else. For each of the 8: keep every limb exactly where the mannequin has it (same joint positions and angles, same lean, same head position, same size and same place in its cell), so the 8 figures stay the same size as each other. BLUE limbs are his LEFT arm and leg; RED limbs are his RIGHT arm and leg; the darker shade is the upper limb, the lighter the lower. He faces and moves toward the viewer's LEFT, seen exactly from the side (his left side toward the viewer, his face in profile). How he does it: he ploughs forward like a bull, upright with his chest and belly pushed out, elbows wide, fists clenched, grinning; the open coat flies out behind him. Each figure has exactly two arms and two legs, and both feet are drawn complete. Wherever his face shows it is fully drawn, with eyes, eyebrows, nose and mouth as on the model sheet: never a blank face. All 8 drawings must be the SAME character with IDENTICAL design, colours and details in every drawing: Tane, a 16-year-old boy, stocky and a bit fat with a soft round belly, warm medium-brown skin and thick eyebrows. HAIR: a tall glossy black pompadour swept up and forward, short at the sides and back. COAT: a long plain dark-red coat down to his calves, always worn open, with a high stand-up collar and long sleeves to the wrists; four round gold buttons in a row down the front edge on HIS RIGHT side and nothing else on it; the back of the coat is plain dark red with one centre seam. BELLY WRAP: a white sleeveless undershirt tucked into a wide white cloth wrap wound round his whole belly from chest to waist, drawn with three or four horizontal fold lines. TROUSERS: plain baggy black trousers gathered at the ankles. FEET: bare feet in wooden geta sandals: a plain light-brown wooden block sole with one black V-shaped strap between the toes. HANDS: bare hands, no gloves, no rings. FACE: round cheeks, thick black eyebrows, a wide fearless grin showing his teeth. No pins, no badges, no emblems, no insignia, no stars, no lettering, no numbers, no logos and no brand marks anywhere on him. No toothpick, no cigarette, no weapon. Remove every trace of the mannequins: no blue, red, green or grey mannequin colour may remain. Style as the second image: 1990s cel anime: bold clean black ink outlines of even weight, flat colour fills, two tones per material (a base and one hard-edged shade), no gradients, no texture, no soft shading, no motion blur, no speed lines, no ground, no shadows on the ground, no text, no panel borders. Background: one flat solid pure magenta (#FF00FF) everywhere, also between the legs and inside every gap. His arms PUMP hard and are different in every drawing, exactly as each mannequin has them: when the near (left, blue) arm swings forward its fist comes up in front of his chest, and when it swings back its elbow is thrown out behind his back with the fist down by his hip, so that in some drawings the near fist is in front of his body and in others it is behind it. The far (right, red) arm does the opposite and shows in front of his chest when the near arm is back. He grins, teeth bared, in every drawing.",
